---
options:
  crash_on_yield: false
---
# Example: Fault Continuation
# Every step of a fair<fault> action is a fault, including the steps after
# its first yield, so they can't be in a counterexample's loop either.
# Once a fault has started, the rest of it is still scheduled fairly, so a
# run can't leave it half done forever.
# Demonstrates: fair<fault> on a serial action with several steps

action Init:
    up = True

serial fair<fault> action Glitch:
    up = False
    up = True

eventually always assertion StaysUp:
    return up
